{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add your app’s own state to every report, so the agent sees what the screenshot can’t show."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/AttachingYourOwnFiles"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/attachingyourownfiles"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Your app knows things ScreenClip can’t see: the signed-in account, what’s in the cart, which feature flags are on, the last request the backend answered. Register an attachment provider and its files travel with every report, next to the built-in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/Diagnostics","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["#if DEBUG","ScreenClipKit.setAttachmentProvider(\"cart\") { context in","  let cart = await MainActor.run { CartStore.shared.snapshot }  \/\/ any Encodable","  return [try .json(cart, name: \"cart\", summary: \"the cart's \\(cart.items.count) items and promo codes\")]","}","#endif"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The agent reads each file’s name and summary in its prompt. It opens a file only when the screenshot and note aren’t enough, so write the summary for it: say what is inside.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Attachment providers need ScreenClipKit 1.2.0 or later.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"When-the-provider-runs","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"When the provider runs"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"With ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Attach logs and diagnostics"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" enabled, the provider starts when the report sheet opens. It can read the app state while the tester annotates. Turning diagnostics on later starts a fresh provider run with the same report ID and capture time.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"After ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Send"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", ScreenClip waits up to ","type":"text"},{"code":"timeout","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" more (5 seconds by default, at most 30) with ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Saving report…"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" on screen. It then sends the report without whatever hasn’t arrived.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The provider runs off the main actor. Read main-actor state with ","type":"text"},{"code":"await MainActor.run { … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and keep heavy work out of that closure.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Several-files-async-work-and-context","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Several files, async work, and context"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A provider returns any number of attachments. Return an empty array to add nothing this time.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["ScreenClipKit.setAttachmentProvider(\"account\", timeout: .seconds(10)) { context in","  let session = await MainActor.run { Session.current }","  guard let session else { return [] }","  let flags = try await FeatureFlags.shared.current()","  APILog.shared.mark(\"ScreenClip report \\(context.reportID)\")","  return [","    try .json(session.debugSummary, name: \"account\", summary: \"signed-in account, plan, and region\"),","    .text(flags.description, name: \"feature-flags\", summary: \"remote feature flags in effect\"),","    .text(await APILog.shared.recent(20), name: \"api-requests\", summary: \"last 20 backend requests and status codes\"),","  ]","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipReportContext","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" carries the report’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"reportID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"capturedAt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"screenTitle","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"screenPath","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Log the report id next to your own records, such as a backend request id or an analytics session, to tie them to the report.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Cancellation-and-failure","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Cancellation and failure"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The provider is cancelled when the tester cancels the report, or turns off "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Attach logs and diagnostics"}]},{"type":"text","text":". Use cancellable APIs or check "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task.isCancelled"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the provider throws or misses its timeout, only its own files are left out. The report is still sent, and a line is logged under the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenClipKit"},{"type":"text","text":" subsystem."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Registering-and-removing","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Registering and removing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each id holds one provider. Registering the same id again replaces it, so calling ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" from an initializer or ","type":"text"},{"code":"onAppear","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is safe. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/removeAttachmentProvider(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" removes it. Providers run concurrently, and their files are listed in registration order.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Names-and-limits","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Names and limits"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name"},{"type":"text","text":" becomes a file name the Mac accepts. It is lowercased, anything other than letters, digits, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"type":"text","text":" becomes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"type":"text","text":", and it is cut to 32 characters, plus "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".txt"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".json"},{"type":"text","text":". A name already in use, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"logs.txt"},{"type":"text","text":" or another provider’s, gets "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-2"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-3"},{"type":"text","text":", and so on."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each attachment can be up to 1 MB ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment\/maximumBytes","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). Larger ones are left out."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A report takes up to 16 attachments ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment\/maximumCount","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). Later ones are left out."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All files in a report share a 4 MB limit. When a report is over it, the largest files are dropped first."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"What-not-to-attach","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"What not to attach"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Don’t attach secrets. On the Mac, token-like strings are hidden in text files, but JSON files are stored as sent. Any attached file can be read by an agent working on the report.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In Release builds ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" does nothing, and the closure is never called. Keep the call inside ","type":"text"},{"code":"#if DEBUG","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" anyway, so the code that gathers the data stays out of Release too.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit"]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ScreenClipKit"}],"title":"Attaching your own files","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Attaching your own data","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)","doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/removeAttachmentProvider(_:)","doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachmentProvider","doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment","doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipReportContext"],"anchor":"Attaching-your-own-data"}],"kind":"article","references":{"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/Diagnostics":{"abstract":[{"text":"The optional files ScreenClipKit attaches, and how the tester controls them.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Diagnostics","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/Diagnostics","url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/diagnostics"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit":{"role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Report what you see in your own iOS app, straight into ScreenClip on your Mac, where a coding agent fixes it."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit","images":[{"identifier":"screenclip-icon.svg","type":"icon"}],"title":"ScreenClipKit","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit","kind":"symbol"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipReportContext":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenClipReportContext"}],"url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipreportcontext","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipReportContext","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"ScreenClipReportContext","abstract":[{"text":"What a provider knows about the report it is attaching to.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenClipReportContext"}]},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipKit/setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"setAttachmentProvider"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"timeout"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Duration"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:13ScreenClipKit0aB18AttachmentProvidera","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ScreenClipAttachmentProvider"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Adds your app’s own files to every report: state, records, anything an agent would want"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to see next to the screenshot."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/setAttachmentProvider(_:timeout:_:)","url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipkit\/setattachmentprovider(_:timeout:_:)"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipKit/removeAttachmentProvider(_:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"removeAttachmentProvider"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Stops adding the files from the provider registered with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"removeAttachmentProvider(_:)","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipKit\/removeAttachmentProvider(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipkit\/removeattachmentprovider(_:)"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipAttachment":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenClipAttachment"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A file your app adds to a report, next to ScreenClip’s own logs and diagnostics."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"ScreenClipAttachment","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenClipAttachment"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment","url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipattachment"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipAttachmentProvider":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenClipAttachmentProvider"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenClipAttachmentProvider"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Collects your app’s own attachments for a report. It runs off the main actor; read main-actor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await MainActor.run { … }"},{"type":"text","text":". Throwing leaves this provider’s files out of the report."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachmentProvider","title":"ScreenClipAttachmentProvider","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipattachmentprovider","kind":"symbol"},"screenclip-icon.svg":{"alt":"The ScreenClip icon","variants":[{"traits":["1x","light"],"url":"\/images\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/screenclip-icon.svg"}],"type":"image","identifier":"screenclip-icon.svg"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipAttachment/maximumCount":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maximumCount"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The most attachments ScreenClip sends with one report, across all providers. Later ones are left out."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"maximumCount","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment\/maximumCount","url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipattachment\/maximumcount"},"doc://com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit/documentation/ScreenClipKit/ScreenClipAttachment/maximumBytes":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maximumBytes"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The largest attachment ScreenClip sends. Larger ones are left out of the report."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mirageteam.screenclip.kit\/documentation\/ScreenClipKit\/ScreenClipAttachment\/maximumBytes","title":"maximumBytes","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/screenclipkit\/screenclipattachment\/maximumbytes","kind":"symbol"}}}